        {
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE:HIGH",
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:Source: The accountName parameter in the injectableQuery method originates from the HTTP request parameter userid. Sink: The query.executeQuery() call on line 69 executes the SQL command. Dataflow: The user-controlled accountName is concatenated directly into the queryString on line 45. While parameters are partially used, the string concatenation for accountName bypasses parameterization, creating an SQL Injection vulnerability. No sanitization is performed on accountName before inclusion in the query. Conclusion: The code is confirmably vulnerable to SQL Injection."
            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-sqli",
          "ruleIndex": 5,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Source: The accountName parameter in the injectableQuery method originates from the HTTP request parameter userid. Sink: The query.executeQuery() call on line 69 executes the SQL command. Dataflow: The user-controlled accountName is concatenated directly into the queryString on line 45. While parameters are partially used, the string concatenation for accountName bypasses parameterization, creating an SQL Injection vulnerability. No sanitization is performed on accountName before inclusion in the query. Conclusion: The code is confirmably vulnerable to SQL Injection."
          },
          "locations": [
