        {
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE:HIGH",
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:Source: The taskAction field is populated via deserialization in readObject through stream.defaultReadObject(). Sink: Runtime.getRuntime().exec(taskAction) at line 69. Dataflow: Data from serialized input is assigned to taskAction and used directly in the exec() method. Sanitization: Although there is a prefix and length check, it does not prevent command injection if an attacker provides a payload like 'ping 127.0.0.1; rm -rf /', which satisfies both constraints. This is a clear command injection vulnerability."
            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-cmdi",
          "ruleIndex": 4,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Source: The taskAction field is populated via deserialization in readObject through stream.defaultReadObject(). Sink: Runtime.getRuntime().exec(taskAction) at line 69. Dataflow: Data from serialized input is assigned to taskAction and used directly in the exec() method. Sanitization: Although there is a prefix and length check, it does not prevent command injection if an attacker provides a payload like 'ping 127.0.0.1; rm -rf /', which satisfies both constraints. This is a clear command injection vulnerability."
          },
