          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE:HIGH",
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:Source: User-provided input via the 'editor' parameter in the @RequestParam annotation. Dataflow: This input is passed into the 'compileFromString' method, where it is embedded into a Java class structure in 'getJavaFileContentsAsString' and then processed by the JavaCompiler. Sink: The 'task.call()' method at line 99 triggers the compilation of this source code. Conclusion: This is a textbook example of arbitrary code execution through dynamic compilation. The application allows an attacker to compile and attempt to execute arbitrary Java code on the server, which facilitates remote code execution."
            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-xpathi",
          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Source: User-provided input via the 'editor' parameter in the @RequestParam annotation. Dataflow: This input is passed into the 'compileFromString' method, where it is embedded into a Java class structure in 'getJavaFileContentsAsString' and then processed by the JavaCompiler. Sink: The 'task.call()' method at line 99 triggers the compilation of this source code. Conclusion: This is a textbook example of arbitrary code execution through dynamic compilation. The application allows an attacker to compile and attempt to execute arbitrary Java code on the server, which facilitates remote code execution."
          },
